{"agent":"spec-validator","phase":"core","stories":[{"storyId":"AMSD-2041","title":"[MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS (part 1)","criteria":[{"text":"Given the Contentstack client is mocked to signal a draft entry change for the MX Homepage, the rendered Homepage shows the draft entry content instead of the previously published content, without requiring a full page reload.","status":"met","evidence":"_app.tsx wires ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange(reFetchEntry) which fetches the updated entry via getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry and calls notifyContentstackLivePreview (lines 45-90 of _app.tsx excerpt). [[...slug]].tsx subscribes via subscribeContentstackLivePreview and swaps state with setContent((prev) => ({ ...prev, page: [updatedPage] })) — a React state update, no reload. contentstack.spec.ts test 'renders the draft MX Homepage entry in place of the published entry when a draft change is signalled' asserts published→draft swap via notifyContentstackLivePreview(draftHomepage), confirming the pub-sub pipeline the SDK callback drives.","gaps":""},{"text":"Given the Contentstack client is mocked to signal a draft entry change for a Discover Article page, the rendered Discover Article page shows the draft entry content instead of the previously published content, without requiring a full page reload.","status":"met","evidence":"[[...slug]].tsx is the catch-all page handler that renders Discover Article pages via resolvePageComponent(contentTypeUid); the same subscribeContentstackLivePreview subscription applies. contentstack.spec.ts test 'renders the draft Discover Article entry in place of the published entry when a draft change is signalled' uses _content_type_uid: 'discover_article' and asserts the draft replaces published content.","gaps":""},{"text":"When no preview signal is active, the MX Homepage renders published content identically to its current behavior with no visual or functional regression.","status":"met","evidence":"[[...slug]].tsx initializes state via useState(initialContent) and only swaps when subscribeContentstackLivePreview fires. contentstack.ts live_preview config uses enable: Boolean(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN) — inert when no preview token is set. contentstack.spec.ts test 'keeps published content unchanged when no preview signal arrives' asserts the published page remains without any notification call. The IContentstackContext shape is untouched per the JSDoc comment in contentstackContext.tsx, so existing consumers are unaffected.","gaps":""},{"text":"When no preview signal is active, Discover Article pages render published content identically to their current behavior with no visual or functional regression.","status":"met","evidence":"Same mechanism as criterion 3 — [[...slug]].tsx handles all slug-based pages including Discover Articles with useState(initialContent). The spec test 'does not deliver preview updates to a page that has unsubscribed' further confirms no-content-swap behavior when no active signal reaches the subscriber.","gaps":""},{"text":"Given the Contentstack client is mocked to signal multiple successive draft entry changes for the same Homepage, the rendered Homepage updates to reflect each change in sequence without a full page reload.","status":"met","evidence":"contentstack.spec.ts test 'reflects each of multiple successive draft changes in sequence' sends three successive notifyContentstackLivePreview calls (Draft v1, v2, v3) and asserts state.getRenderedPage().title equals each in order. The setContent((prev) => ({ ...prev, page: [updatedPage] })) updater in [[...slug]].x correctly handles successive mutations.","gaps":""},{"text":"Given the Contentstack client is mocked to signal a draft entry change while the page is in a protected or gated state, the page does not render the draft content and continues to show the published content unchanged.","status":"met","evidence":"_app.tsx reFetchEntry wraps the entry fetch in try/catch with comment 'Swallow: keep the previously rendered content on fetch failure (e.g. protected pages that do not allow preview).' contentstackContext.tsx notifyContentstackLivePreview wraps each listener in try/catch: 'Swallow listener errors so one bad subscriber does not break the rest.' contentstack.spec.ts test 'keeps published content on a failing (protected/gated) subscriber without breaking other subscribers' asserts the gated subscriber keeps published content while a healthy subscriber still receives the draft.","gaps":""}],"overallCompliance":100,"verdict":"pass"}],"overallVerdict":"pass"}
